lumn 0, Column 2. This gives middle row and bottom row, left and right columns. Positions shown 1,2 for rows, 0,2 columns. Missing 0 for rows. Eh.\n\nHonestly any 4 works. Let me do row0, row1, col0, col1 to show top and middle rows, left and middle columns, and the \"tile\" direction for both axes. Missing bottom row and right column.\n\nI'll just choose: row0, row2, col0, col2. Clean and symmetric.\n\nLet me build inputs.\n\nRow0 uniform:\n[3,3,3]\n[1,2,4]\n[5,6,7]\n\nRow2 uniform:\n[1,4,7]\n[2,5,8]\n[9,9,9]\n\nCol0 uniform:\n[4,1,2]\n[4,3,5]\n[4,6,7]\n\nCol2 uniform:\n[1,2,6]\n[3,4,6]\n[5,7,6]\n\nLet me call show_transformed_input for each. I can make multiple calls in one block.\n\nLet me double check the verifier for row0 uniform: i=0, np.all(input[0]==input[0,0]) -> all 3 equal 3 -> true. output rows 0:3 = tile(input,(1,3)). tile horizontally 3 copies. Yes matches example.\n\nGood. Let me submit.",
